{"headline":"SEC calls out refs for missing Oklahoma's 'hideout tactic'","description":"The SEC vowed \"appropriate accountability\" after it said officials failed to identify a \"hideout tactic\" on Oklahoma's second-quarter touchdown against Auburn.","published":"2025-09-21T16:17:44.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/46330363/sec-calls-refs-missing-oklahoma-hideout-tactic","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eli Lederman","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Indiana starting guard Brunner out for season with ACL injury","description":"Indiana starting guard Joe Brunner will miss the rest of the season after sustaining an ACL injury in Thursday's practice, coach Curt Cignetti said on Monday.","published":"2026-11-16T18:20:25.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50503016/indiana-starting-guard-brunner-season-acl-injury","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"NC State hires Jatavis Sanders as GM under Philip Rivers","description":"NC State has hired Jatavis Sanders as its general manager under new coach Philip Rivers, the school announced Monday.","published":"2026-11-16T16:33:25.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50502157/nc-state-hires-jatavis-sanders-gm-philip-rivers","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Max Olson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"ACC suspends Louisville LB Clark, UNC DB Smith over postgame brawl","description":"The ACC has suspended Louisville LB Stanquan Clark and North Carolina DB Greg Smith III, while also issuing fines and public reprimands to both schools in the wake of Saturday's postgame brawl.","published":"2026-11-16T16:19:01.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50502075/louisville-lb-clark-unc-db-smith-suspended-postgame-brawl","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Michigan top WR JJ Buchanan (shoulder) likely out for season","description":"Michigan's leading receiver JJ Buchanan will likely miss the rest of the season after he sustained a shoulder injury in Saturday's loss at No. 16 Oregon.","published":"2026-11-16T16:30:02.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50502065/michigan-top-wr-jj-buchanan-shoulder-likely-season","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2026 college football coaching carousel: Tracking every open job","description":"As the carousel spins, we'll keep you updated with all the comings and goings.","published":"2026-11-16T16:00:31.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50358611/2026-cfb-coaching-carousel-firings-hirings","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"UTEP fires head coach Scotty Walden following 8th straight loss","description":"The UTEP Miners, just 1-9 this season and mired in an eight-game losing streak, have fired head coach Scotty Walden, the school announced Monday.","published":"2026-11-16T15:13:07.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50501672/utep-1-9-season-fires-coach-walden-8th-straight-loss","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Max Olson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Where is 'College GameDay'? 2026 schedule, locations, recaps","description":"What is the \"College GameDay\" schedule? Find out more about where the program will be each week of the 2026 college football season.","published":"2026-11-16T14:25:23.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/49783645/where-college-gameday-2026-schedule-locations-recaps","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5080703/isaiah-sategna-iii","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isaiah_Sategna_III"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Isaiah Sategna III","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isaiah_Sategna_III","description":"American football player (born 2003)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:15Z","intro":"Isaiah Sategna III (born July 11, 2003) is an American college football wide receiver for the Oklahoma Sooners. He previously played for the Arkansas Razorbacks.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Sategna III attended Fayetteville High School in Fayetteville, Arkansas. As a senior, he had 100 receptions for a nation-leading 1,908 yards and 17 touchdowns. For his career, he had 172 receptions for 3,261 receiving yards and 25 touchdowns. Sategna III originally committed to Texas A&M University and the University of Oregon before ultimately choosing the University of Arkansas."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"In his first year at Arkansas in 2022, he redshirted after appearing in four games and recording two receptions for 12 yards. In 2023, he appeared in 12 games with one start and had 15 receptions for 129 yards with two touchdowns and 23 kick returns for 500 yards and 15 punt returns for 180 yards and one touchdown. In 2024, he started 10 of 12 games, finishing with 37 receptions for 491 yards with a touchdown. After the season, Sategna transferred to the University of Oklahoma. For the 2025 season, Sategna led OU in receptions (67), receiving yards (965), and receiving touchdowns (8) and was named 1st team All-SEC. The Sooners finished the season 10-3 after losing to Alabama in the first round of the playoffs. Sategna will return to Oklahoma for his senior season in 2026."}]}}